window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["tr-11.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">الشرح الأصلي بالإنكليزية.</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> ابحث بالرمز أو بالاسم الإنكليزي. تأكد من نوع ناقل الحركة بسيارتك قبل ما تتبع دليل معيّن.</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">OVERVIEW</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION The Borg Warner 44-40 is a full time All Wheel Drive (AWD) transfer case with a fixed gear ratio. Depending on traction conditions, the Powertrain Control Module (PCM) will modulate the electromagnetic clutch assembly to vary the amount of torque applied to the front axle. Torque is transmitted through the input shaft to the clutch and drive sprocket assembly, and is transferred directly to the rear propeller shaft, and to the output shaft and front propeller shaft by the drive chain. The oil pump circulates gear lube throughout the case to provide clutch cooling, and the Drivetrain Control Module (DTCM) monitors the temperature of the transfer case with a temperature sensor.</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ADJUSTMENTS</strong><small>الضبط</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Install the oil pump (7), the new clutch assembly (1), the rotor (2), the bearing (6), and the spacer (5) on the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install the (special tool #10177, Nut, Lockdown) (3) on the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Set up a dial indicator (4) to measure the clearance between the rotor (2) and the top clutch disc inside the clutch housing (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Zero the dial indicator (4).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Push the rotor (2) downward evenly as close to the shaft as possible and record the highest reading. Repeat this measurement in three more locations and calculate the average of all four measurements. This is the total amount of clutch clearance.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>The total clutch clearance must be between 1.2 mm and 0.7 mm (0.047 in. and 0.028 in.). If the total clutch clearance is not within specifications, select a larger or smaller spacer as needed, and re-check clutch clearance.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS</strong><small>المواصفات الفنية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS</strong><small>عزوم الشد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><pre class=\"en-pre\">          DESCRIPTION                N.m          Ft. Lbs.        In. Lbs.            COMMENT\nCase Bolts                            31             23               -                  \nSnubber Bolts                          8              -              71                  \nOil Baffle Bolts                       8              -              71                  \nDrain Plug                            23             17               -                  \nFill Plug                             23             17               -                  \nClutch Coil Nuts                      10              -              89                  \nRear Output Flange Nut               319            235               -                  \nTransfer Case To Transmission\n                                      55             41               -                     \nBolts\nRear Transfer Case Cover              31             23               -                     </pre></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">GENERAL SPECIFICATIONS</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><pre class=\"en-pre\">GENERAL SPECIFICATIONS\n          DESCRIPTION                           Metric                           Standard\n          Clutch Clearance                 0.7 mm - 1.2 mm                   0.028 in. - 0.047 in.\n  Clutch Coil Resistance @ 20° C\n                                                             2.85 - 3.15 ?\n              (68° F)\n  Temperature Sensor Resistance @\n                                                             2726 - 3603 ?\n          20° C (68° F)</pre><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">REMOVAL</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Raise and support the vehicle. Refer to HOISTING, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the transfer case drain plug (2) and allow the transfer case lubricant to drain into a suitable container.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove the exhaust. Refer to MUFFLER, EXHAUST, REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove the rear drive shaft. Refer to REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Disconnect the temperature sensor wire harness connector (1) and the clutch coil wire harness connector (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Raise transmission slightly with service jack to relieve load on crossmember and supports.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Remove bolts (2) securing rear support and cushion to transmission crossmember (3).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Remove bolts attaching the crossmember (1) to frame and remove crossmember (3).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Remove the front drive shaft. Refer to REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The front (transmission) side of the transfer case flange is shown for clarity.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Remove the lower transfer case to transmission bolts from the lower half of the transfer case flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Slightly lower the rear of the transmission to gain access to the upper transfer case to transmission bolts.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Support the transfer case with a transmission jack</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Remove the upper transfer case to transmission bolts from the upper half of the transfer case flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Remove the transfer case.</span></div></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DISASSEMBLY</strong><small>التفكيك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         The vent hole is near the input shaft hub. If the unit is set on the mounting surface, oil will drain out through the vent.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the drain plug (2) and drain any remaining fluid from the transfer case.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install the (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove the rear output flange washer (1)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Remove the outer rear output shaft seal (1)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Remove the rear output flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Remove the transfer case bolts.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The clutch rotor might remain in the rear transfer case half during removal.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Remove the rear transfer case half (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Remove the spacer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Remove the bearing (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Remove the clutch rotor (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Remove the ball bearings (1) from the apply cam (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Remove the apply cam (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Remove the wave spring (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Remove the snap ring (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>Remove the clutch assembly (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>Remove the thrust washer (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The output shaft sprocket is pressed onto the output shaft.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>Release the snap ring (1) from the output shaft and move it away from the groove (3), toward the output shaft sprocket (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span>Slide the Front Drive Sprocket Remover (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) (1) in between the case and the input shaft sprocket (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">20</span><span>Align the holes on the Front Drive Sprocket Remover (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Puller Plate (1) with the bolt holes in the output shaft flange (2), then install the Front Drive Sprocket Remover (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Puller Plate (1) onto the output shaft flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">21</span><span>Install the Front Drive Sprocket Remover (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Base (1) onto the puller plate.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Install the Front Drive Sprocket Remover (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) (1) so that the bearing flange is facing up.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">22</span><span>Install the Front Drive Sprocket Remover (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Bearing (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">23</span><span>Install the Front Drive Sprocket Remover (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">24</span><span>Tighten the nut until the output shaft (1) is pulled free of the output shaft sprocket.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">25</span><span>Remove the output shaft sprocket, the drive chain, and the drive sprocket as an assembly.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">26</span><span>Remove the input shaft assembly (1) from the front transfer case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The top spacer (6) might remain attached to the drive sprocket when it is removed from the input shaft (1).</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">27</span><span>Remove the top spacer (6) from the input shaft (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">28</span><span>Remove the bearing (1) and the bottom spacer (2) from the input shaft (3).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">29</span><span>Remove the oil pump assembly (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">30</span><span>Remove the transfer case magnet (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">31</span><span>Use the (special tool #9585, Remover, Bearing Cup) Bearing Cup Remover (1) and (special tool #C-637, Slide Hammer, Universal) Slide Hammer (2) to remove the output shaft bearing (3) from the rear transfer case half.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">32</span><span>Use the (special tool #9585, Remover, Bearing Cup) Bearing Cup Remover (1) and (special tool #C-637, Slide Hammer, Universal) Slide Hammer (2) to remove the input shaft bearing from the rear transfer case half.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">33</span><span>Use the (special tool #9585, Remover, Bearing Cup) Bearing Cup Remover (1) and (special tool #C-637, Slide Hammer, Universal) Slide Hammer (2) to remove the output shaft bearing (3) from the front transfer case half (4).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">34</span><span>Use the (special tool #9664, Remover, Bearing Cup) Bearing Cup Remover and (special tool #C-637, Slide Hammer, Universal) Slide Hammer to remove the input shaft bearing from the front transfer case half.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">35</span><span>Remove the tie straps, and remove the convoluted sheath from the clutch coil wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">36</span><span>Remove the retainer (1) from the clutch coil wire harness connector (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The clutch coil wires are retained in the wire harness connector by tabs. The tabs must be released from the connector face to remove the wires from the wire harness connector.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">37</span><span>Remove the cover (1) from the clutch coil wire harness connector (2), release the tabs, and disconnect the clutch coil terminal ends from the clutch coil wire harness connector (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">38</span><span>Remove the clutch coil retainers (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">39</span><span>Remove the clutch coil (1) from the rear transfer case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">40</span><span>Remove the fastener (4) and the oil baffle (5).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">41</span><span>Remove the fasteners (1) and (2) and the snubbers (3).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">42</span><span>Remove the input and output shaft seals from the front transfer case half.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">43</span><span>Remove the input shaft seal from the rear transfer case half.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">ASSEMBLY</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check the clearance for the new clutch pack, and select a new spacer if necessary. Refer to ADJUSTMENTS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Position the rear transfer case half (3) on a suitable arbor press, and position the (special tool #8835-3, Receiver, Bushing) Bushing Receiver (1) to support the rear transfer case half (3) from below in the area of the output shaft bearing.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Use the (special tool #8441-2, Cup, Receiver) Receiver Cup (2) and an arbor press to install the output shaft bearing into the rear transfer case half (3).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Use the (special tool #D-156, Installer, Bearing) Bearing Installer (1) and an arbor press to install the input shaft bearing (2) into the rear transfer case half (3).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Install the snubbers (3), the snubber bolts (1, 2) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Install the oil baffle (5), the oil baffle bolts (4) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Route the wires through the rear transfer case half (2) and install the clutch coil (1) into the rear transfer case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Install the clutch coil nuts (1) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Install clutch coil wire terminal ends into the clutch coil wire harness connector (2), engage the terminal ends in the tabs, then install the cover (1).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            If the original convoluted sheath is damaged, install new convoluted sheath</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Install the convoluted sheath and install new tie straps to secure it in position.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Install the wire retainer (1) on the back of the clutch coil wire harness connector (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Position the front transfer case half (1) on an arbor press, and position (special tool #8149, Installer, Seal) Seal Installer (2) to support the input shaft seal flange from below.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Use (special tool #8153, Installer, Bearing Cup) Bearing Installer (1) and an arbor press to install the input shaft bearing (2) into the front transfer case half.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Use (special tool #10174, Installer, Seal, Rear Output) Rear Output Seal Installer to install the rear input shaft seal into the rear transfer case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Use (special tool #10173, Installer, Input Shaft Seal) Input Shaft Seal Installer (1) to install the front input shaft seal into the front transfer case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>Use (special tool #10174, Installer, Seal, Rear Output) Rear Output Seal Installer to install the rear output shaft seal into the front transfer case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>Use the (special tool #D-156, Installer, Bearing) Bearing Installer and an arbor press to install the output shaft bearing into the front case half.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>Install the transfer case magnet (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span>Position the oil pump assembly (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">20</span><span>Slide the oil pump down until it fully engages the splines (2) on the input shaft (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">21</span><span>Install the bottom spacer (4), the bearing (5), and top spacer (6) onto the input shaft (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">22</span><span>Install the input shaft assembly (1) into the front transfer case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The output shaft sprocket is pressed onto the output shaft.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the snap ring (1) is temporarily installed too close to the top of the output shaft, it might not be possible to install it into the bottom groove on the output shaft after the output shaft sprocket is pressed onto the output shaft.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">23</span><span>Temporarily install the snap ring (1) approximately 3 mm (0.12 in.) above the groove (3) on the output shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">24</span><span>Install the output shaft sprocket, the drive chain and the drive sprocket as an assembly.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           When the output shaft sprocket (2) is at the correct height, the top groove</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">(1) on the output shaft will be visible.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">25</span><span>Use the (special tool #8835-3, Receiver, Bushing) Bushing Receiver and a suitable arbor press to install the output shaft sprocket (2) onto the output shaft. Press the sprocket until the top groove (1) on the output shaft is visible.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">26</span><span>Press the output shaft upward with the output shaft flange, then install the snap ring (1) into the groove (3) on the output shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">27</span><span>Install the thrust washer (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">28</span><span>Install a new clutch assembly (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">29</span><span>Install the snap ring (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">30</span><span>Install the wave spring (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">31</span><span>Install the apply cam (2), and the ball bearings (1)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">32</span><span>Install the clutch rotor (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">33</span><span>Install the bearing (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">34</span><span>Install the spacer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">35</span><span>Apply a bead of Loctite® 598 HB to the front transfer case half sealing surface.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">36</span><span>Install the rear transfer case half (1), rear transfer case half bolts and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">37</span><span>Install the rear output flange (1)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">38</span><span>Install a new outer rear output shaft seal (1)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">39</span><span>Install the rear output flange washer (1)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">40</span><span>Install the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">41</span><span>Install (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) (1) onto the rear output flange (2). Tighten the rear output flange nut to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">INSTALLATION</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using a transmission jack, and raise the transfer case up to the rear transmission flange.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Align the transfer case dowel pins with the holes in the rear transmission flange.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The front (transmission) side of the transfer case flange is shown for clarity.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install the transfer case to transmission bolts (1, 2) and tighten the transfer case to transmission bolts to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Raise the transfer case and transmission up into position, and support with a suitable service jack. Remove the transmission jack.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Install the front propeller shaft. Refer to INSTALLATION .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Install the crossmember (3) and install the bolts attaching the crossmember (1) to frame.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Lower transmission with service jack onto crossmember and supports.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Install the bolts (2) securing rear support and cushion to transmission crossmember (3).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Connect the temperature sensor wire harness connector (1) and the clutch coil wire harness connector (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Install the rear propeller shaft. Refer to INSTALLATION .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Install the exhaust. Refer to MUFFLER, EXHAUST, INSTALLATION .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>If the fluid was drained, fill the transfer case with proper amount and type of fluid. Refer to CAPACITIES AND RECOMMENDED FLUIDS, SPECIFICATIONS .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Remove the support and lower the vehicle.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">SPECIAL TOOLS</strong><small>العدد الخاصة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">10173 - Installer, Input Shaft Seal (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 10175.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">10174 - Installer, Seal, Rear Output (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 10175.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">10176 - Remover, Front Drive Sprocket (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 10175.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">6958 - Wrench, Spanner (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 6947, 6949, 6966, 8204, 8204CC, 8667.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">8149 - Installer, Seal (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 8104A.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">8153 - Installer, Bearing Cup (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 8104.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">8441-2 - Cup, Receiver (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 8665, 8665CC, 8702.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">8835-3 - Receiver, Bushing (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 8715, 8719.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">9585 - Remove(Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9691.)r, Bearing Cup</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">9664 - Remover, Bearing Cup (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9675, 9685, 9695.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">C-637 - Slide Hammer, Universal (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 9202.)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">D-156 - Installer, Bearing (Originally Shipped In Kit Number(s) 8207, 8418.)</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">CHAIN</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the transfer case from the vehicle. Refer to REMOVAL.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         The vent hole is near the input shaft hub. If the unit is set on the mounting</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">surface, oil will drain out through the vent.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the drain plug (2) and drain the remaining fluid.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Remove the rear output flange washer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Remove the outer rear output shaft seal (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Remove the rear output flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Remove the transfer case half bolts.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The clutch rotor might remain in the rear transfer case half during removal.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Remove the rear transfer case half (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Remove the spacer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Remove the bearing (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Remove the clutch rotor (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Remove the ball bearings (1) from the apply cam (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Remove the apply cam (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Remove the wave spring (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>Remove the snap ring (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>Remove the clutch assembly (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>Remove the thrust washer (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The output shaft sprocket is pressed onto the output shaft.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span>Release the snap ring (1) from the output shaft and move it away from the groove (3), toward the output shaft sprocket (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">20</span><span>Slide the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) in between the case and the input shaft sprocket (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">21</span><span>Align the holes on the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) with the bolt holes in the output shaft flange (2), then install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) onto the output shaft flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">22</span><span>Install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) onto the puller plate.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) so that the bearing flange is facing up.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">23</span><span>Install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">24</span><span>Install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">25</span><span>Tighten the nut until the output shaft (1) is pulled free of the output shaft sprocket.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">26</span><span>Remove the output shaft sprocket, the drive chain, and the drive sprocket as an assembly.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTALLATION</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        The output shaft sprocket is pressed onto the output shaft.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        If the snap ring (1) is temporarily installed too close to the top of the output shaft, it might not be possible to install it into the bottom groove on the output shaft after the output shaft sprocket is pressed onto the output shaft.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Temporarily install the snap ring (1) approximately 3 mm (0.12 in.) above the groove (3) on the output shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install the output shaft sprocket, the drive chain and the drive sprocket as an assembly.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           When the output shaft sprocket (2) is at the correct height, the top groove (1) on the output shaft will be visible.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Use the (special tool #8835-3, Receiver, Bushing) Bushing Receiver and an arbor press to install the output shaft sprocket (2) onto the output shaft. press the sprocket until the top groove (1) on the output shaft is visible.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Press the output shaft upward with the output shaft flange, then install the snap ring (1) into the groove (3) on the output shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Install the thrust washer (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            If installing a new clutch pack, check the clutch pack clearance, and select a new spacer if necessary. Refer to ADJUSTMENTS.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">6.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Install the clutch assembly (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Install the snap ring (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Install the wave spring (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Install the apply cam (2), and the ball bearings (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Install the clutch rotor (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Install the bearing (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Install the spacer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Apply a bead of Loctite® 598 HB to the front case half sealing surface.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Install the rear transfer case half (1) and tighten the rear transfer case bolts to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>Install the rear output flange (1)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>Install a new outer rear output shaft seal (1)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>Install the rear output flange washer (1)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span>Install the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">20</span><span>Install (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2). Tighten the rear output flange nut to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">21</span><span>Install the transfer case. Refer to INSTALLATION.</span></div></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">CLUTCH</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the transfer case. Refer to REMOVAL.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The vent hole is near the input shaft hub. If the unit is set on the mounting surface, oil will drain out through the vent.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Place the transfer case so that it can be drained of any remaining fluid and remove the drain plug (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Remove the rear output flange washer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Remove the outer rear output shaft seal (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Remove the rear output flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Remove the transfer case half bolts.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Remove the rear transfer half (1).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The clutch rotor might remain in the rear transfer case half during removal.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Remove the spacer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Remove the bearing (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Remove the clutch rotor (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Remove the ball bearings (1) from the apply cam (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Remove the apply cam (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Remove the wave spring (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>Remove the snap ring (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>Remove the clutch assembly (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTALLATION</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>If installing a new clutch pack, check the clutch pack clearance, and select a new spacer if necessary.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Refer to ADJUSTMENTS.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install the clutch assembly (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install the snap ring (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install the wave spring (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Install the apply cam (2), and the ball bearings (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Install the clutch rotor (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Install the bearing (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Install the spacer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Apply a bead of Loctite® 598 HB to the front case half sealing surface.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Install the rear transfer case half (1). Tighten the rear transfer case half bolts to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Install the rear output flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Install a new outer rear output shaft seal (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Install the rear output flange washer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Install the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Install (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2). Tighten the rear output flange nut to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>Install the transfer case. Refer to INSTALLATION.</span></div></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">COIL, CLUTCH</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the transfer case. Refer to REMOVAL.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The vent hole is near the input shaft hub. If the unit is set on the mounting surface, oil will drain out through the vent.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the drain plug (2) and drain the remaining fluid from the transfer case.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Remove the rear output flange washer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Remove the outer rear output shaft seal (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Remove the rear output flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Remove the transfer case half bolts.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Remove the rear transfer case half (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Remove the tie straps, and remove the convoluted sheath from the clutch coil wires.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Remove the retainer (1) from the clutch coil wire harness connector (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The clutch coil wires are retained in the wire harness connector by tabs. The tabs must be released from the connector face to remove the wires from the wire harness connector.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Remove the cover (1) from the clutch coil wire harness connector (2), release the tabs, and disconnect the clutch coil terminal ends from the clutch coil wire harness connector (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Remove the clutch coil retainers (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Remove the clutch coil (1) from the rear transfer case half (2).</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTALLATION</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Route the wires through the rear transfer case half (2) and install the clutch coil (1) into the rear transfer case half.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install the clutch coil retainers (1) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install clutch coil wire terminal ends into the clutch coil wire harness connector (2), engage the terminal ends in the tabs, then install the cover (1).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            If the original convoluted sheath is damaged, install new convoluted sheath</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install the convoluted sheath and install new tie straps to secure it in position.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Install the wire retainer (1) on the back of the clutch coil wire harness connector (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Install the rear transfer case half (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Install the rear transfer case half bolts and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Install the rear output flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Install the outer rear output shaft seal (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Install the rear output flange washer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Install the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Install (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2) and tighten the rear output flange nut to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Install the transfer case. Refer to INSTALLATION.</span></div></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">FLUID</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">STANDARD PROCEDURE</strong><small>إجراء قياسي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">FLUID CHECK</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Raise and support the vehicle. Refer to HOISTING, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Clean the area around the transfer case fill (3) and drain plugs (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            Inspect all the transfer case plug seals and replace as necessary.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove the transfer case fill plug (3).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove the transfer case drain plug (2) and allow the transfer case lubricant to drain into a suitable container.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>When the fluid has stopped draining, install the drain plug (2) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Using the fill hole (3), fill the transfer case with 1.0 L +/- 0.05 L (2.11pint +/- 0.11 pint) of fluid. Refer to CAPACITIES AND RECOMMENDED FLUIDS, SPECIFICATIONS .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Install the fill plug (3) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">PUMP, TRANSMISSION OIL</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the transfer case. Refer to REMOVAL.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The vent hole is near the input shaft hub. If the unit is set on the mounting surface, oil will drain out through the vent.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the drain plug (2) and drain the remaining fluid from the transfer case.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Remove the rear output flange washer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Remove the outer rear output shaft seal (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Remove the rear output flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Remove the transfer case half bolts.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The clutch rotor might remain in the rear transfer case half during removal.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Remove the rear transfer case half (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Remove the spacer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Remove the bearing (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Remove the clutch rotor (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Remove the ball bearings (1) from the apply cam (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Remove the apply cam (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Remove the wave spring (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>Remove the snap ring (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>Remove the clutch assembly (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>Remove the thrust washer (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The output shaft sprocket is pressed onto the output shaft.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span>Release the snap ring (1) from the output shaft and move it away from the groove (3), toward the output shaft sprocket (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">20</span><span>Slide the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) in between the case and the input shaft sprocket (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">21</span><span>Align the holes on the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) with the bolt holes in the output shaft flange (2), then install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) onto the output shaft flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">22</span><span>Install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) onto the puller plate.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) so that the bearing flange is facing up.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">23</span><span>Install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">24</span><span>Install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">25</span><span>Tighten the nut until the output shaft (1) is pulled free of the output shaft sprocket.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">26</span><span>Remove the output shaft sprocket, the drive chain, and the drive sprocket as an assembly.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">27</span><span>Remove the input shaft assembly (1) from the front case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The top spacer (6) might remain attached to the drive sprocket when it is removed from the input shaft (1).</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">28</span><span>Remove the top spacer (6) from the input shaft (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">29</span><span>Remove the bearing (1) and the bottom spacer (2) from the input shaft (3).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">30</span><span>Remove the oil pump assembly (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTALLATION</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Position the oil pump assembly (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Slide the oil pump down until it fully engages the splines (2) on the input shaft (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install the bottom spacer (4), the bearing (5), and top spacer (6) onto the input shaft (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install the input shaft assembly (1) into the front transfer case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The output shaft sprocket is pressed onto the output shaft.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the snap ring (1) is temporarily installed too close to the top of the output shaft, it might not be possible to install it into the bottom groove on the output shaft after the output shaft sprocket is pressed onto the output shaft.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Temporarily install the snap ring (1) approximately 3 mm (0.12 in.) above the groove (3) on the output shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Install the output shaft sprocket, the drive chain and the drive sprocket as an assembly.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            When the output shaft sprocket (2) is at the correct height, the top groove (1) on the output shaft will be visible.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Use the (special tool #8835-3, Receiver, Bushing) Bushing Receiver and a suitable arbor press to install the output shaft sprocket (2) onto the output shaft. Press the sprocket until the top groove (1) on the output shaft is visible.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Press the output shaft upward with the output shaft flange, then install the snap ring (1) into the groove (3) on the output shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Install the thrust washer (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Install the clutch assembly (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Install the snap ring (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Install the wave spring (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Install the apply cam (2), and the ball bearings (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Install the clutch rotor (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Install the bearing (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>Install the spacer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>Apply a bead of Loctite® 598 HB to the front case half sealing surface.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>Install the rear transfer case half and the bolts and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span>Install the rear output flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">20</span><span>Install a new outer rear output shaft seal (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">21</span><span>Install the rear output flange washer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">22</span><span>Install the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">23</span><span>Install (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2) and tighten the rear output flange nut to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">24</span><span>Install the transfer case. Refer to INSTALLATION.</span></div></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">SEAL, INPUT SHAFT</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">FRONT</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the transfer case. Refer to REMOVAL.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the front input shaft seal.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REAR</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the rear propeller shaft. Refer to REMOVAL .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove the rear output flange washer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Remove the outer rear output shaft seal (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Remove the rear output flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Remove the inner rear input shaft seal.</span></div></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTALLATION</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">FRONT</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use (special tool #10173, Installer, Input Shaft Seal) Input Shaft Seal Installer (1) to install the front input shaft seal into the front case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install the transfer case. Refer to INSTALLATION.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REAR</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use (special tool #10174, Installer, Seal, Rear Output) Rear Output Seal Installer (1) to install the rear input shaft seal into the rear transfer case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install the rear output flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install the outer rear output shaft seal (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install the rear output flange washer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Install the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Install (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2) and tighten the rear output flange nut to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Install the rear propeller shaft. Refer to INSTALLATION .</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">SEAL, OUTPUT SHAFT</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Remove the transfer case. Refer to REMOVAL.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The vent hole is near the input shaft hub. If the unit is set on the mounting surface, oil will drain out through the vent.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Remove the drain plug (2) and drain the remaining fluid from the transfer case.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Install the (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Remove the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Remove the rear output flange washer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Remove the outer rear output shaft seal (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Remove the rear output flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Remove the transfer case half bolts.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The clutch rotor might remain in the rear transfer case half during removal.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Remove the rear transfer case half (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Remove the spacer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Remove the bearing (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Remove the clutch rotor (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Remove the ball bearings (1) from the apply cam (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Remove the apply cam (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Remove the wave spring (1) from the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>Remove the snap ring (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>Remove the clutch assembly (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>Remove the thrust washer (1) from the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The output shaft sprocket is pressed onto the output shaft.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span>Release the snap ring (1) from the output shaft and move it away from the groove (3), toward the output shaft sprocket (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">20</span><span>Slide the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) in between the case and the input shaft sprocket (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">21</span><span>Align the holes on the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) with the bolt holes in the output shaft flange (2), then install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) onto the output shaft flange (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">22</span><span>Install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) onto the puller plate.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1) so that the bearing flange is facing up.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">23</span><span>Install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">24</span><span>Install the (special tool #10176, Remover, Front Drive Sprocket) Front Drive Sprocket Remover (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">25</span><span>Tighten the nut until the output shaft (1) is pulled free of the output shaft sprocket.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">26</span><span>Remove the output shaft sprocket, the drive chain, and the drive sprocket as an assembly.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">27</span><span>Remove the input shaft assembly (1) from the front transfer case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">28</span><span>Remove the output shaft seal.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTALLATION</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Use the (special tool #10174, Installer, Seal, Rear Output) to install the output shaft seal into the front case half.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Install the input shaft assembly (1) into the front case half (2).</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The output shaft sprocket is pressed onto the output shaft.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            If the snap ring (1) is temporarily installed too close to the top of the output shaft, it might not be possible to install it into the bottom groove on the output shaft after the output shaft sprocket is pressed onto the output shaft.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Temporarily install the snap ring (1) approximately 3 mm (0.12 in.) above the groove (3) on the output</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">shaft.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Install the output shaft sprocket, the drive chain and the drive sprocket as an assembly.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           When the output shaft sprocket (2) is at the correct height, the top groove (1) on the output shaft will be visible.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Use the (special tool #8835-3, Receiver, Bushing) Bushing Receiver and a suitable arbor press to install the output shaft sprocket (2) onto the output shaft. Press the sprocket until the top groove (1) on the output shaft is visible.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Press the output shaft upward with the output shaft flange, then install the snap ring (1) into the groove (3) on the output shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Install the thrust washer (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>Install the clutch assembly (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">9</span><span>Install the snap ring (1) onto the input shaft (2).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">10</span><span>Install the wave spring (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">11</span><span>Install the apply cam (2), and the ball bearings (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">12</span><span>Install the clutch rotor (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">13</span><span>Install the bearing (1) onto the input shaft.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">14</span><span>Install the spacer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span>Apply a bead of Loctite® 598 HB to the front case half sealing surface.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">16</span><span>Install the rear transfer case half (1) and bolts and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">17</span><span>Install the rear output flange (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">18</span><span>Install a new outer rear output shaft seal (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">19</span><span>Install the rear output flange washer (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">20</span><span>Install the rear output flange nut.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">21</span><span>Install the (special tool #6958, Wrench, Spanner) Spanner Wrench (1) onto the rear output flange (2) and tighten to the proper torque specifications. Refer to TORQUE SPECIFICATIONS.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">22</span><span>Install the transfer case. Refer to INSTALLATION.</span></div></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">15</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">SENSOR, TRANSFER CASE TEMPERATURE</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">REMOVAL</strong><small>الفك</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Raise and support the vehicle. Refer to HOISTING, STANDARD PROCEDURE .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the wire harness connector from the Transfer Case Temperature sensor (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Remove the Transfer Case Temperature sensor (4) from the Transfer Case housing.</span></div></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTALLATION</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">INSTALLATION</strong><small>التركيب</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Replace the Transfer Case Temperature sensor with pre-applied sealant to the threads.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Tighten the Transfer Case Temperature sensor (4).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Connect the temperature sensor wire harness connector (1).</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>If any fluid was drained, fill the transfer case with proper amount and type of fluid. Refer to CAPACITIES AND RECOMMENDED FLUIDS, SPECIFICATIONS .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Lower the vehicle and remove the support.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910348</p></div></div></details></div></details>";
